{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class cf111c {\n    private static int rows, cols, maskLimit;\n    private static int[][][] stateDP;\n    private static int[] population;\n\n    private static int bitCount(int num) {\n        int count = 0;\n        while (num > 0) {\n            count++;\n            num &= num - 1;\n        }\n        return count;\n    }\n\n    private static boolean fullyCovered(int top, int mid, int bot) {\n        int coverage = (maskLimit - 1) & (mid | (mid << 1) | (mid >> 1) | top | bot);\n        return coverage == maskLimit - 1;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        rows = scanner.nextInt();\n        cols = scanner.nextInt();\n        if (rows < cols) {\n            int swap = rows;\n            rows = cols;\n            cols = swap;\n        }\n\n        maskLimit = 1 << cols;\n        stateDP = new int[rows + 1][maskLimit][maskLimit];\n        population = new int[maskLimit];\n\n        for (int i = 0; i <= rows; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < maskLimit; j++) {\n                Arrays.fill(stateDP[i][j], 999);\n            }\n        }\n\n        for (int state = 0; state < maskLimit; state++) {\n            population[state] = bitCount(state);\n            stateDP[0][0][state] = 0;\n        }\n\n        for (int layer = 1; layer <= rows; layer++) {\n            for (int curState = 0; curState < maskLimit; curState++) {\n                for (int prevState = 0; prevState < maskLimit; prevState++) {\n                    for (int prevPrevState = 0; prevPrevState < maskLimit; prevPrevState++) {\n                        if (stateDP[layer - 1][prevPrevState][prevState] != 999 && \n                            fullyCovered(prevPrevState, prevState, curState)) {\n                            stateDP[layer][prevState][curState] = Math.min(\n                                stateDP[layer][prevState][curState],\n                                stateDP[layer - 1][prevPrevState][prevState] + population[prevState]\n                            );\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        int optimal = 999;\n        for (int endState = 0; endState < maskLimit; endState++) {\n            optimal = Math.min(optimal, stateDP[rows][endState][0]);\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(rows * cols - optimal);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nint bitCount(int num) {\n    int count = 0;\n    while (num > 0) {\n        count++;\n        num &= num - 1;\n    }\n    return count;\n}\n\nbool fullyCovered(int top, int mid, int bot, int maskLimit) {\n    int coverage = (maskLimit - 1) & (mid | (mid << 1) | (mid >> 1) | top | bot);\n    return coverage == maskLimit - 1;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int rows, cols;\n    cin >> rows >> cols;\n    \n    if